{"availability":"available","full":"FreeMason9226/governed-autonomy-substrate","name":"governed-autonomy-substrate","description":"Governed Autonomy Substrate is a modular Substrate-based framework for building governed autonomous systems. It bundles runtime pallets, node configs, Helm charts, tests, and docs to support cluster sandboxing, CI workflows, and real-world deployments with reproducible infrastructure and developer tooling.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Python","stars":2,"forks":2,"created":"2026-09-22T04:33:14Z","updated":"2026-10-08T08:34:57Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://freemason9226.github.io/governed-autonomy-substrate/","topics":[],"demo":"https://freemason9226.github.io/governed-autonomy-substrate/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T15:04:41.688Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T15:04:41.688Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T15:04:41.688Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T06:39:34.956Z","stars":2,"forks":2},{"at":"2026-10-10T15:04:41.688Z","stars":2,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A cryptographic authorization barrier for AI agents: no signed artifact, no action. Every action must carry a short-lived, single-use, Ed25519-signed Governance Authorization Artifact (GAA) that matches an audited, hash-chained log entry and the current policy.","Despite the repository name, this project currently implements a Python governance service and worker; it does not contain Polkadot/Substrate runtime pallets. OPA/Rego is used for pull-request risk scoring, while runtime action authorization is enforced by the Python policy engine."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/FreeMason9226/governed-autonomy-substrate/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4faf6272a0c816e23823e82cfc712d48af70c3b1ef6c37d39c7027e24ebdd269","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T11:47:39.538Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T11:47:39.538Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A cryp